title: Command line
kind: overview
aliases: cli
summary: mf, a thin client over the daemon — one daemon, one repository per call, the same verbs at every level.

`mf` is the command-line client. It does no database or watching work itself:
every command is a call to the [[Daemon]], which must be running. The daemon and
the repository are chosen once per call, by options that come before the command
([[Global options]]); the commands form a tree of nouns and verbs whose verbs mean
the same thing at every level ([[The verb pattern]]).

```
mf -n music metarecord -q 'rating > 3' field set reviewed:bool=true
```

`mf --help` lists the commands, and every command has its `--help`; each one also
has its note here, under [[CLI command]].

